package sparq:instrument@1.1.0;

// sparq instrument contract — the world (WO-017 freeze set)
//
// Status: v0 SKELETON. What an instrument component is, in one declaration: it imports four
// host services and exports one guest interface. Nothing else — no WASI imports, no ambient
// authority, no wasi:io/wasi:clocks preopens. Capability-scoping (ADR-010 decision 2) is
// expressed by the ABSENCE of imports as much as by the manifest's [capabilities] table:
// what is not in this world does not exist for a guest.
//
// The world is named for the tier, not the company: a backbone module never becomes a wasm
// component (T1 is native by the ADR-002 admission rule), so `instrument` is the only world
// this package ships. If a future contract needs a second world (e.g. a display-only companion
// component), it arrives as a new world in a MINOR — additive, like everything else.

world instrument {
  /// design tokens at runtime (control-thread; fetched at prepare)
  import tokens;

  /// clocks, seed tree, diagnostics, api version
  import host;

  /// capability-scoped asset reads (control-thread)
  import assets;

  /// bound stream snapshots for displays (UI-thread)
  import sources;

  /// lifecycle + process + draw
  export guest;
}
